{"title":"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagram shows an octagon consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> unit squares. The portion below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> is a unit square and a triangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> bisects the area of the octagon, what is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d00b56616d287ad0ad42eb93bb47b8600bfe56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{XQ}{QY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"41\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bba290e642b0a44220ce1e8ce69c823fe134b28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(300);  real lsf = 0.5;  pen dp = linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(10);  defaultpen(dp);  pen ds = black;  pen xdxdff = rgb(0.49,0.49,1); draw((0,0)--(6,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((0,0)--(0,1),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((0,1)--(1,1),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((1,1)--(1,2),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((1,2)--(5,2),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((5,2)--(5,1),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((5,1)--(6,1),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((6,1)--(6,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((1,1)--(5,1),linewidth(1.2pt)); draw((1,1)--(1,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((2,2)--(2,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((3,2)--(3,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((4,2)--(4,0),linewidth(1.2pt));  draw((5,1)--(5,0),linewidth(1.2pt)); draw((0,0)--(5,1.5),linewidth(1.2pt)); dot((0,0),ds); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, (-0.23,-0.26),NE*lsf);  dot((0,1),ds);  dot((1,1),ds);  dot((1,2),ds);  dot((5,2),ds);  label(&quot;$X$&quot;, (5.14,2.02),NE*lsf); dot((5,1),ds);  label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, (5.12,1.14),NE*lsf); dot((6,1),ds);  dot((6,0),ds); dot((1,0),ds); dot((2,0),ds); dot((3,0),ds);  dot((4,0),ds); dot((5,0),ds); dot((2,2),ds); dot((3,2),ds);  dot((4,2),ds); dot((5,1.5),ds);  label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, (5.14,1.51),NE*lsf);  clip((-4.19,-5.52)--(-4.19,6.5)--(10.08,6.5)--(10.08,-5.52)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"505\" height=\"202\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/398a6b319ac29a95ab2e5788e74df5e8c845e77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that half the area of the octagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We see that the triangle area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/3580a3c7e4b8c340c96073d0fd2038e4eaa05010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. That means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61af019651c9cc971ecbae358efc916289e4a9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5h}{2} = 4 \\rightarrow h=\\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51e67a5af29dec7181d654c8f9db251979e609e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{QY}=\\frac{8}{5} - 1 = \\frac{3}{5}\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"37\" />\nMeaning, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/355f599ea3f9582320040b2d9333b0111400856b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{2}{5}}{\\frac{3}{5}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"99\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like stated in solution 1, we know that half the area of the octagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>After moving the square from the bottom right to the top left, the area of the resulting trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be26679d50e3af55de40859c96ddcfe1ff151bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+1=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/063b87dc9bed52aa1773196a247bb3598bc1b457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(XQ+2)/2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fb543400533dbfcf7bccdee3b618bcdc49faf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c5167061861bab8a986407b06b0ef58ae1a42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XQ=2/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f568e6598e1bdb1664691a4dcbb263ad2b0e9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a7ea7197d08c01a1af42d174b14cecb19d4695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QY=3/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer comes out to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25bb5ce191a564ea576ffe37db4b07f91e22db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~kempwood\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=937\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=937</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_MathTalks\">Video by MathTalks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video by MathTalks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KSYVsSJDX-0&amp;feature=youtu.be\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KSYVsSJDX-0&amp;feature=youtu.be</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/N7Yu9-bLqls\">https://youtu.be/N7Yu9-bLqls</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 8\">2010 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2010\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl